# Storage

Separate responsibilities across five layers.

## 1. Source Preservation Layer

Stores original and derived source artifacts.

Examples: manuscript images, PDFs, audio, video, OCR output, transcripts, translations, imported commentary texts.

Best fit: Object storage (MinIO, S3).

## 2. Structured Governance Layer

Stores governed objects whose lifecycle, identity, and review state matter.

Examples: works, witnesses, segments, units, claims, evidence records, provenance records, commentary identities, editorial states, version history.

Best fit: PostgreSQL.

## 3. Ontology And Relation Layer

Stores reusable semantic entities and governed relations.

Examples: themes, symbols, concepts, human experiences, literary devices, traditions, ontology aliases, merge lineage, semantic relations.

Best fit: Neo4j.

## 4. Commentary Document Layer

Stores composed human-readable knowledge artifacts.

Examples: unit commentary documents, work commentary documents, question-centered commentary, tradition-specific commentary.

Best fit: Document-oriented storage or structured files with durable identifiers.

## 5. Semantic Retrieval Layer

Stores representations used for embedding search and retrieval-time AI assistance.

Examples: embeddings, retrieval chunks, semantic summaries, vector indexes, retrieval hints.

Best fit: Qdrant.

Nothing should ever be discarded. Always preserve original source, parsed source, extracted entities, embeddings, and knowledge graph.

